    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46046" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑωσφόρος</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀωσφόρος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Bringer of morn,
				the Morning-star</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				23.226
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				381
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>I.</u>
				4(3).24
			</span></i>; 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕσπερος</span>
			 and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀφροδίτης ἀστήρ</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Ibyc.
				42
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				38d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eudox.
				<u>Ars</u>
				5.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Placit.</u>
				2.15.4
			</span></i>. (Trisyll. in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
			</span></i>, quadrisyll. in <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
			</span></i> (s.v.l.): <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀεσφόρος</span> (cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐασφόρος</span>) is cj. in <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
			</span></i> l.c.)</div>
